# Techno Sapiens Conventions

STOP. Before writing code or suggesting changes, apply these conventions.

## Naming

### Files

* PHP (non-class): `kebab-case.php`
* PHP classes: `PascalCaseFileName.php` (e.g. `SectionContent.php`)
* Section JS: `kebab-case.js` (e.g. `section-content.js`)
* Shared JS classes/features: `camelCase.js` or PascalCase class files in `js/lib/`
* SCSS: `kebab-case.scss` (e.g. `section-content.scss`)
* Images: `kebab-case.jpg` or `icon-close.svg`

### Sections (page builder)

Page layouts are **section-based ACF blocks**, not column-based blocks. Canonical example: `sections/section-content`.

* **Directory:** `sections/section-content/` (`section-` prefix + kebab-case)
* **PHP class:** `SectionContent.php`
* **`SECTION_ID`:** `section_section_content` (`section_` + slug with underscores)
* **`SECTION_SLUG`:** `section-content` — used for `has_block('acf/section-' . self::SECTION_SLUG)`, ACF location, webpack keys, partials
* **ACF `name`:** `self::SECTION_ID` (no `acf/` prefix)
* **ACF JSON:** `acf-json/section-content.json` (filename = `SECTION_SLUG`)
* **Partial:** `partials/section-content.php`
* **SCSS:** `scss/section-content.scss`
* **JS (only if needed):** `js/section-content.js`

Do not create new blocks under `blocks/`. Use `sections/`.

### Functions, variables, PHP

* Functions start with a verb. Avoid obscure abbreviations.
* Variables: camelCase. Constants: `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE`.
* **Namespace:** `TechnoSapiens`
* Classes: `PascalCaseClassName`
* Methods: `public static function camelCaseMethod($args): void`

## Comments

* Explain *why*, not what the code already shows.
* Comments go on the line(s) **before** the code. No inline comments.
* Do not narrate edits in comments. Use git commits.

## Debugging

Use `TechnoSapiens\Core\Log::log`. Maximum two arguments. Prefer an associative array:

```php
Log::log([
    'message' => 'Checking combination',
    'type' => $combinationType,
    'price' => $shippingPrice
]);
```

## Styling

* BEM, one element level: `section-content__text`, not `section-content__text__link`.
* Modifiers: `section-content__text--bg-white` or `section-content--bg-white`.
* CSS variables: `var(--ts-...)` from `StylingComponent.php`.
* Never use hex fallbacks. Use named color fallbacks: `var(--ts-color-primary, red)`.

## Images

Follow [070-image-handling.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/070-image-handling.mdc). Use `TechnoSapiens\Core\Image::render()`. Match `section-content` (image field as array, then `ID`).

## Responsive

Breakpoints: xs, sm, md, lg, xl, xxl. Prefer `mq-up` (see [050-responsive-media-queries.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/050-responsive-media-queries.mdc)). `mq-down` only when the design needs it (as in `section-content`).

## Performance

Load section CSS/JS only when the section is on the page. Webpack keys come from `SECTION_SLUG`. Guard empty manifest URLs.

## Security

Validate input. Escape output ([030-php-html-templating.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/030-php-html-templating.mdc)).

